<p>Most freelancers set their rate by looking at what competitors charge, picking a number that feels comfortable, or dividing their old salary by 2,080. All three approaches leave money on the table — or worse, set a rate that doesn't cover your actual costs.</p>

<p>Here's how to calculate a rate that's grounded in math, not guesswork.</p>

